// error
// #4491: a plain `x = y` assignment was never checked for assignability at
// all. `vStmt`'s Tag.Assign arm had `vDestructure` (arity), `vAssignIface`
// (interface targets only) and `vCompoundAssign` (`+=`), and no general
// verdict — so every non-interface `lhs = rhs` was accepted whatever the two
// types were, and lowering reinterpreted the bits. This program exited 0 and
// printed `4342972592`: the `[]string` header's address read as an i64.
//
// The control that always worked, and is what makes this a gap rather than a
// design: passing `ys` to `fn take(v: []int)` is E0041 on the same two types.
fn main() {
  let xs = []int(0)
  xs = append(xs, 1)
  let ys = []string(0)
  ys = append(ys, "a")
  let p = xs
  p = ys
  print("${p[0]}\n")
}
